# Prompt-To-Native-VR: core rules

- This project is **local-first** and targets a **native C++ VR executable**
  running on Windows PC VR (Meta Quest 3 via Quest Link).
- **Do NOT introduce** Unity, Unreal Engine, Godot, WebXR, Three.js,
  Babylon.js, or any browser-rendered VR runtime.
- Rendering uses **Vulkan**. XR uses **OpenXR**. Build is **CMake** with
  **vcpkg manifest mode**.
- Do not add cloud services: no Supabase, S3, Temporal, cloud auth, multiplayer,
  speech-to-text, marketplace publishing, Steam packaging, Quest standalone
  packaging in this version.
- Prefer determinism over agent improvisation. Prefer reusable built-in VR
  mechanics over regenerating them.
- Whenever you change the set of artifacts, stages, providers, or engine
  subsystems, update `docs/` in the same change.
- Before editing provider code, verify SDK signatures and model names against
  official docs.
